+# The tasks board
+
+Asked for at the 12 November meeting (item 5): get the task sheet onto a board so the
+Thursday meeting stops being a read-through. Following `pattern.md`, its layout comes from
+what the committee said the sheet fails at, not from the events board.
+
+## What it has to do, and where each need came from
+
+| Need | Source | What the board does |
+|---|---|---|
+| Stop reading through 40 lines to reach what's due by next Thursday | 12 Nov, item 1 | First section: everything overdue or due by the next Thursday meeting |
+| "I just want to know what's mine this week" | 12 Nov, item 1 (Ines) | One fold per person, showing only their open tasks, with overdue and due-this-week flagged |
+| Done tasks out of the way | 12 Nov, item 1 (Tomas) | Done tasks only appear in a closed fold at the bottom |
+| Jobs with nobody on them (water meter, shed gutter since July, lost property) | 29 Oct items 3–4, 12 Nov items 2 and 4 | Section "Nobody's name on it" near the top |
+| Several jobs stuck with the council; Priya is finding the contact | 5 Nov item 4, mail thread | "Waiting on someone else", grouped by who it's waiting on |
+| The polytunnel rota, so swaps are written where everyone can see them | 29 Oct item 2, 12 Nov item 3 | Rota section from this week on; empty weeks say "nobody yet" |
+| Quantities (manure loads) visible so nobody double-orders | 5 Nov item 3 | Quantity shown on the task line |
+| Readable on a phone without scrolling sideways | 29 Oct item 5 (Hal) | One column, no table |
+
+## Data
+
+The board reads `incoming/tasks.csv` directly. The page is rebuilt from that export and
+never edited by hand, so there's no copy inside the board folder to fall out of step with
+it. The export's quirks are tidied up when the page is built, not in the file, because
+next week's export will have the same quirks: status is matched whatever its case
+(`Done`), and a name typed all in lower case gets a capital letter (`priya`).
+
+The rota uses the sheet's last two columns (`water_week`, `water_who`). Those columns
+don't belong to the task on the same row; they just share the sheet.
+
+## Checks (written before the board was built)
+
+The board ships iff every one of these holds on the page built from the current export,
+with "today" set to 17 Nov 2026:
+
+1. No task marked done (any case) shows outside the Done fold. The fold counts 6.
+2. "Before Thursday 19 Nov" holds exactly the open tasks due on or before 19 Nov, and
+   the shed gutter (due 30 Sep) is marked overdue.
+3. "Nobody's name on it" lists all 5 open tasks with no name.
+4. Each person's fold lists exactly their open tasks; `priya`'s seed potatoes are under Priya.
+5. Waiting-on groups: council has 5 open tasks; the streetlight (done) isn't among them.
+6. The rota starts at the week of 16 Nov (Tomas), and 21 Dec shows "nobody yet".
+7. Order manure shows quantity 3.
+8. The page has no `<table>` and keeps the same narrow single-column style as the events board.
+9. `python3 kit/board.py boards/events` still produces the same events page as before.
+
+Correction, made before the board was built: checks 1 and 3 first said 7 and 6. Those were
+miscounts; counting the export gives 6 done tasks and 5 open tasks with no name.
